   "source": [
    "# ⚡ BookError — Interactive Out-of-Order Execution Demo\n",
    "\n",
    "Welcome to the **BookError** demo notebook!\n",
    "\n",
    "### What this notebook demonstrates:\n",
    "1. **Execution Tracking**: BookError tracks cell executions and variable reads/writes in real time.\n",
    "2. **Out-of-Order Error Tracing**: When Cell 4 drops the `'age'` column and Cell 5 tries to access it, BookError traces the exact causal chain.\n",
    "3. **Scikit-Learn Style Pipeline Banner**: Generates an interactive visual flow directly inside the cell output block."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "🔍 BookError active. Tracking cell executions.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Step 1: Load the BookError IPython extension\n",
    "%load_ext bookerrror\n",
    "import pandas as pd"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Step 2: Load data into DataFrame\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv('demo/data.csv')\n",
    "df.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Step 3: Out-of-Order mutation — Drop column 'age'\n",
    "df = df.drop(columns=['age'])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Step 4: Access dropped column 'age'\n",
    "# Running this cell raises KeyError: 'age' and triggers BookError's Scikit-Learn style pipeline visualizer!\n",
    "result = df[['age', 'income']]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Step 5: Render dependency SVG graph widget\n",
    "from bookerrror.presentation import render_graph_view\n",
    "from bookerrror.tracer import trace_error\n",
    "from IPython.display import get_ipython\n",
    "\n",
    "tracker = getattr(get_ipython(), '_bookerrror_tracker', None)\n",
    "if tracker and tracker.graph.records:\
    path = trace_error(tracker.graph, KeyError(\"'age'\"))\n",
    "    render_graph_view(path)"
   ]
  }
 ],
